---
title: "pipecat eval"
sidebarTitle: "eval"
description: "pipecat eval runs scenario evals against a running agent."
---

Run scenario-based evals.

## eval run

**Usage:**

```shell
pipecat eval run [OPTIONS] SCENARIOS...
```

**Arguments:**

<ParamField path="SCENARIOS..." type="path" required>
  Scenario files. A positional argument, not an option.
</ParamField>

**Options:**

<ParamField path="--bot-url" type="string" default="ws://localhost:7860/ws">
  Agent URL.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--verbose" type="flag">
  cli-missing-option: the page leaves out `-v`.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--timeout / -t" type="integer" default="30">
  cli-default-mismatch: the code's default is a constant equal to 60.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--record-dir" type="string" default="recordings">
  Recordings directory.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--legacy-mode" type="flag">
  cli-unmarked-deprecation: its help starts with "Deprecated".
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--old-flag" type="flag" deprecated>
  Marked, so not a cli-unmarked-deprecation.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--retries" type="integer" default="3.0">
  An `Annotated` option. 3.0 and 3 are the same number.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--bogus-flag" type="flag">
  cli-stale-option: the command has no such option.
</ParamField>

## eval suite

**Options:**

<ParamField path="--pattern / -p" type="string">
  Scenario glob.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="--concurrency" type="integer" default="4">
  Agents at a time.
</ParamField>
